{
  "description": "Canonical test vector for the plausibility check on a climb Ascend did not measure. The same cases pin the Swift implementation (AscendApp/Shared/Models/ClimbPacePolicy.swift), the TypeScript derivation (maxAverageStepsPerMinute and parseEligibleWorkout in functions/src/leaderboardStats.ts) and the Firestore rules refusal line (isPhysicallyPossibleClimb in firestore.rules, five steps a second), so the three cannot drift. verdict is ClimbPacePolicy.verdict; saveable is whether the device lets the climb be saved; deviceLeaderboardStatus is what ClimbPacePolicy.leaderboardStatus stores on the device; serverCountsOnLeaderboards is whether parseEligibleWorkout derives the climb into a standing. A live climb keeps the 220 steps a minute sensor gate and is never marked excluded on the device.",
